.TH "LMM" "1" "Oct 2026" "lmm 2.2.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-launch - Launch the game


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm launch [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch the game for its active profile.

.PP
lmm uses the first launch method that applies:
.IP "  1." 5
launch.command in games.yaml: that program, with its arguments.
.IP "  2." 5
A Steam app id: steam steam://rungameid/<id> (through the Flatpak
 Steam for a game in its library, or xdg-open when steam is not
 installed). The id is launch.steam_app_id, else the game's
 steamworkshop source, else the Steam library the game is installed
 in - so a game added from Steam launches with nothing configured.

.PP
launch.via in games.yaml picks one method instead.

.PP
The game starts as a transient systemd user service (systemd-run --user),
so it does not belong to lmm: closing the terminal or restarting
\&'lmm serve' leaves it running. With no systemd user manager, lmm starts
it detached instead. lmm returns at once; through Steam, success means
Steam was asked to start the game.

.PP
Only the active profile can be launched: -p/--profile naming any other
profile is refused. Make it active first with 'lmm profile switch'.

.PP
When the profile has changes that are not deployed - a mod enabled but
not deployed, or deployed but disabled - lmm warns and launches anyway.
--deploy deploys the profile first; --strict refuses instead. A deploy
does not take down a disabled mod that is still deployed ('lmm profile
apply' does), so --deploy --strict refuses that before deploying.

.PP
Use --dry-run to print the method and the full command line without
starting anything.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm launch --game valheim
  lmm launch --game valheim --deploy
  lmm launch --game valheim --dry-run


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--deploy\fP[=false]
	deploy the profile before launching

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print how the game would be launched without starting it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for launch

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile; only the active profile can be launched (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB--strict\fP[=false]
	refuse to launch when the profile has undeployed changes


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


